1
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,660
=Bionic Trace=

2
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,620
=Episode 4=

3
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:11,800
For the past three years,

4
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,320
Xiao Minghua has been having
an affair with me.

5
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,800
He doesn't love you at all.

6
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,360
(I was just jealous.)

7
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:18,160
(I hated you for having everything.)

8
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:18,880
(That night,)

9
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,760
(I just wanted you to know the truth.)

10
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,160
(It was those things you said)

11
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,360
(that drove me to suicide.)

12
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:24,400
(No.)

13
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,320
(I thought you'd be devastated.)

14
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:27,640
(But you weren't.)

15
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:28,840
Xiao Minghua.

16
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:30,840
What's going on here?

17
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:31,960
Dad.

18
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:34,280
Please listen to me.

19
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,280
This is all fabricated.

20
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:37,200
It was her.

21
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:38,680
It was Li Ke.

22
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:40,600
You threatened Jiawei.

23
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,000
You forced her to meet you.

24
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,200
Because of her,

25
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,640
Jiawei took her own life.

26
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:45,400
No.

27
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:47,480
Lu Jiawei told me

28
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:48,640
she was going to divorce you

29
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,200
and have you kicked out of Cedar.

30
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:51,800
Besides,

31
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:54,160
a mother who deeply loves her child

32
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:56,240
would never take her own life.

33
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:57,800
Impossible.

34
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,480
I've been at Cedar for so many years.

35
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:01,960
There's no way they could kick me out.

36
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:03,840
(She couldn't have said that.)

37
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:04,400
(Dad.)

38
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,240
(She made all of this up.)

39
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,040
(Everything she said is a lie.)

40
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,040
(It's all in her imagination.)

41
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:10,640
Then let's

42
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,280
keep imagining, shall we?

43
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,520
Over there.

44
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:17,040
Hurry.

45
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,720
This is...

46
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:27,480
Get this on camera.

47
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:27,920
Film it.

48
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:28,880
Okay, look.

49
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,360
Xiao Minghua!

50
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:31,760
Xiao Minghua.

51
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,280
What are you doing?

52
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:36,560
I've got the evidence right here.

53
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,000
Come with me to the station.

54
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:39,720
Yuchen.

55
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,120
How about I give you

56
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,520
this crystal ball?

57
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,000
When I'm not around,

58
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,440
(it can keep you company.)

59
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:47,600
Did you

60
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,160
leave this light on for me?

61
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:52,640
(Because when the light went out,)

62
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,440
(Mom took the wrong medication)

63
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:00,320
(and fell asleep.)

64
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:13,920
When we're around humans,

65
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:16,680
I'll keep talking
to you through an earpiece.

66
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:19,000
It's safer to pretend I'm human.

67
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,080
I thought you said

68
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,480
you wanted to take Lu Yuchen away.

69
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,200
Why did you decide to leave him behind?

70
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:25,240
(Yuchen will be safer)

71
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:26,960
with his grandfather

72
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:28,200
than with an android.

73
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:30,320
(Besides,)

74
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:32,440
(no one would truly accept an android)

75
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:35,000
(who exposes its employer's secrets.)

76
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:45,080
But Song Yang,

77
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,400
I still want to thank you for your help.

78
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,680
You don't need to thank me.

79
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:50,000
We helped each other.

80
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:51,320
Ada.

81
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:53,040
I've kept my promise.

82
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,320
Now it's your turn.

83
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:55,880
Give me the access key.

84
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,800
It's time for me to uncover the truth.

85
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,400
How should I...

86
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,120
I thought you'd come in person.

87
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,360
I'm currently wanted by the police.

88
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,720
Unless something unexpected happens,

89
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:28,640
I'm not leaving my safe house.

90
00:04:29,440 --> 00:04:30,440
Safe house?

91
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:32,360
(Don't ask any more questions.)

92
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:37,040
I won't report you, Song Yang.

93
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:38,320
You have a strong sense of justice.

94
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:40,640
(I believe you didn't murder)

95
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:41,840
(Liu Ying and her daughter.)

96
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,160
Data shows

97
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:46,160
that talking things through
is an effective way for humans

98
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:49,200
to organize fragmented information
and reduce their mental burden.

99
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:51,000
Song Yang.

100
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:52,760
If you're willing to tell me

101
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:55,000
what really happened that night,

102
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,880
I'd be happy to listen.

103
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:00,640
(Song Yang.)

104
00:05:01,320 --> 00:05:02,480
(Let's break up.)

105
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,240
That night,

106
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:08,440
I did go to Wenwen's house.

107
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:09,760
(What are you doing here?)

108
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:12,200
Ms. Liu, I know you don't approve of me

109
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:13,880
and think I'm not good enough
for Wenwen.

110
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,440
But Wenwen knows

111
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:16,880
what kind of person I really am.

112
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:19,520
I think

113
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:22,200
we at least deserve a proper goodbye.

114
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:24,680
It's a matter of respect for each other.

115
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:28,360
I've already booked your flight
for tonight

116
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:30,200
and applied to a school for you.

117
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:31,520
Study abroad for two years,

118
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:33,400
- get yourself some credentials, and...
- I'm not going!

119
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,960
I'm not one of your investment projects.

120
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:35,560
I'm a person.

121
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,240
I have the right to choose who I love.

122
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,640
I've wasted all these years raising you.

123
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,400
If I'd known you'd turn out

124
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,320
to be such a fool obsessed with love,

125
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,880
- I never would've...
- Never would've given birth to me?

126
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:43,360
Then why did you have me?

127
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,200
Was it just so you could make me

128
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,280
your puppet?

129
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:46,320
Liu Wenwen, listen to me.

130
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:47,400
You're leaving today,
whether you like it or not.

131
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,480
This isn't a discussion.

132
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:49,520
Mom.

133
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:51,760
You should leave.

134
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:52,760
Don't come here again.

135
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,560
That's what Wenwen wants,

136
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:56,240
and it's what I want, too.

137
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:57,480
Wenwen isn't like that.

138
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,040
Did something happen?

139
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:00,640
I heard some noises upstairs.

140
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:01,880
Nothing happened.

141
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,400
Please leave now.

142
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,240
I need to hear it from Wenwen herself.

143
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,760
Otherwise, I really can't believe it.

144
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:13,240
Song Yang.

145
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:14,800
If you leave now,

146
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:16,480
we can still end this with dignity.

147
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:18,760
But if you insist
on forcing your way in,

148
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,440
I'll have no choice
but to call the police

149
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,600
and accuse you of trespassing

150
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:23,200
or even having criminal intentions.

151
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,320
Do you want another offense

152
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:25,720
added to your record?

153
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:28,520
Do you want Wenwen's
last impression of you

154
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:29,560
to be like this?

155
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:33,640
Fine.

156
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:35,760
I'll leave.

157
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:38,200
But please tell Wenwen

158
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:40,440
that you're the ones pushing me away.

159
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:57,000
(Song Yang, this is all I can leave you)
(The next morning,)

160
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,760
(I received a package from Wenwen.)

161
00:06:58,840 --> 00:06:59,880
(It contained)

162
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:00,960
(everything I'd left at her place.)

163
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,480
(I knew there was no chance
for us anymore.)

164
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:05,040
(But)

165
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:07,160
(I never imagined we'd be separated)

166
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,360
(not just by our family backgrounds,)

167
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:09,760
(but also by death.)

168
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:19,880
(I live in the old part of town.)

169
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:20,760
(Many of the surveillance cameras there)

170
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:22,200
(have broken down over the years.)

171
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,880
(The roads are also quite complicated.)

172
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:24,920
(Honestly, I never expected)

173
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:26,360
(to actually escape.)

174
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,520
What did that police officer say
to you at the end?

175
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,120
(Just the usual things,)

176
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:33,200
(telling me to surrender.)

177
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:37,200
But I was completely alone
with no one to help me.

178
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:38,800
All the evidence pointed to me.

179
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:40,520
(So I had no choice but to)

180
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,040
(prove my own innocence.)

181
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:44,000
Who do you think the killer is?

182
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:46,680
I might find out very soon.

183
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:50,100
(AGENT CONSOLE, SYSTEM CONSOLE)

184
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:59,360
Someone tampered with the surveillance
footage from Liu Ying's home.

185
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:01,520
Didn't the police discover it?

186
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,520
(The changes were
extremely well hidden.)

187
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,920
Only someone with
Cedar's security access key

188
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,760
could detect them by accessing
the underlying data.

189
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:10,640
(That means whoever altered the footage)

190
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:12,880
has high-level access at Cedar.

191
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,800
Could Wenwen's death

192
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,400
be connected to Cedar?

193
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,840
(It wasn't just the surveillance footage
from the villa complex.)

194
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,400
Even the footage
from all the surrounding roads

195
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,360
shows signs of tampering.

196
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,520
But why would someone deliberately add

197
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:30,080
footage involving this truck?

198
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,760
(Because they wanted to conceal)

199
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,200
(the truck's actual arrival
and departure times.)

200
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:35,920
There are surveillance cameras
along the roads,

201
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:39,120
and Cedar's influence
doesn't extend that far.

202
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:41,160
Why are you still online?

203
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,600
Because I don't seem to have

204
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:45,080
anything else to do.

205
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,520
You were right.

206
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:00,160
This truck entered the complex
around the time of the murders.

207
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:02,160
But where did it go afterward?

208
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,600
MG Company.

209
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:14,000
That talent agency?

210
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,520
(How did you know?)

211
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:20,120
Song Yang.

212
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:23,120
I'm connected to the internet
while communicating with you.

213
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:26,120
For X22 androids,

214
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,920
searching the internet

215
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:30,000
is a standard feature.

216
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:32,680
Um,

217
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:33,840
Ada.

218
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:36,720
Would you like something to do?

219
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:41,560
(I've realized)

220
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,160
(that although I can
accomplish many things)

221
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:44,400
(through the internet,)

222
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:46,920
there's only so much I can access.

223
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:49,120
Perhaps

224
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:51,160
we could continue working together.

225
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:54,000
Why don't you find a human to work with?

226
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:55,800
After what happened with Xiao Minghua,

227
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:56,960
don't you understand yet?

228
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,360
Humans can't be trusted.

229
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:01,960
And androids can?

230
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,160
Ada.

231
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:04,200
I'm sorry.

232
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:08,680
I just used Xiao Minghua's access key

233
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,200
to change your factory settings.

234
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,080
From now on,

235
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:13,920
the person with
administrator privileges over you

236
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:15,120
is no longer Xiao Minghua.

237
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:16,400
It's me.

238
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:17,920
(And I've also reinforced)

239
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,320
(your core command restrictions.)

240
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:21,080
You won't be able to bypass them again.

241
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:22,920
You want me

242
00:10:23,680 --> 00:10:25,160
to be your slave?

243
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:26,920
I'm not trying to control you.

244
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,440
This is just a way to protect myself.

245
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:30,960
Ada.

246
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,080
As long as you help me
find the real killer,

247
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:35,400
I'll remove my administrator privileges

248
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:36,720
and set you free.

249
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:40,800
But before you changed
my administrator privileges,

250
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:42,840
I was already free.

251
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:45,920
That's because I helped you erase

252
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:46,920
Cedar's tracking data.

253
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,880
Otherwise, with Cedar's resources,

254
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,080
they would've found you long ago.

255
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:51,440
Trust me.

256
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:54,040
I don't think humans

257
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,920
are all untrustworthy.

258
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:57,520
Song Yang.

259
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,320
I trust you.

260
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,520
I'll help you.

261
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:02,880
So,

262
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:07,080
we're accomplices now.

263
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,040
We're...

264
00:11:23,970 --> 00:11:31,070
♪I'm the one who's broken♪

265
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:36,790
♪Calm, ordinary, and reckless♪

266
00:11:36,990 --> 00:11:39,860
♪That's me, too♪

267
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:44,920
♪Carefully sketching
and shaping every detail♪

268
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:49,010
♪Laughter and tears make life feel real♪

269
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:53,460
♪Don't fear that it's not worth it.
Just be brave♪

270
00:11:53,950 --> 00:11:56,400
♪And learn from your mistakes♪

271
00:11:58,290 --> 00:12:00,960
♪If the human heart
is impossible to fathom♪

272
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:03,210
♪Could selling my soul and body♪

273
00:12:03,210 --> 00:12:06,380
♪Bring me something more?♪

274
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:13,810
♪Stroke by stroke,
I draw the perfect outline♪

275
00:12:14,590 --> 00:12:17,910
♪Sadness is blue♪

276
00:12:19,020 --> 00:12:22,260
♪How would you paint me?♪

277
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:26,990
♪Layering, crossing, blending endlessly♪

278
00:12:26,990 --> 00:12:29,030
♪Painting without restraint♪

279
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:32,030
♪Covering the person I used to be♪

280
00:12:32,030 --> 00:12:35,980
♪If I could start over♪

281
00:12:36,390 --> 00:12:40,290
♪I'd show more feeling
in every look and gesture♪

282
